From: Ruslan Shevchenko <rshevchenko@neoflex.ru>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/i915/dp: prefer DSC over eDP color depths below 8 bpc

The uncompressed link search may select 6 bpc to fit an eDP mode even
when the panel supports a higher input depth with DSC. Since that
configuration is valid, the existing fallback never tries DSC.

Try DSC when a valid uncompressed eDP configuration falls below 8 bpc
and below the permitted input depth. Restore the original pipe_bpp
before computing DSC limits so the uncompressed search does not limit
the DSC input depth.

If DSC configuration or the final dotclock check fails, restore the
uncompressed configuration. Save the complete DSC state, including
compression_enabled_on_link, which intel_dp_dsc_reset_config() does
not clear. Required DSC configurations retain their existing errors.

On a HONOR MagicBook Pro 14, this changes 3120x2080 at 120 Hz from
18 bpp with dithering to 24 bpp with DSC and no dithering.

Based on Ruslan Shevchenko's original eDP DSC preference patch. The
preference policy and restoration of the requested input depth are
retained from that work.

Subsequent changes by NeroSong (2026-09-16):
- Restore the complete DSC state and fec_enable on optional DSC failure,
  including compression_enabled_on_link after a late dotclock rejection.
- Rebase onto the Omarchy 7.2.5 display code and shorten inline comments
  without changing the tested control flow.
- Integrate the patch into the base and BORE kernel package recipes.

Validation:
- Hardware-tested on a HONOR MagicBook Pro 14 with linux-omarchy 7.2.5-3
  using a rebuilt xe module: normal boot, 3120x2080 at 120 Hz, 24 bpp,
  DSC enabled and dithering disabled. Initial external-display hotplug
  also worked. This revision preserves that tested executable logic.
- Ten extracted-function tests cover policy and failure recovery using
  stubbed hardware helpers. The late-dotclock rollback regression fails
  with the original reset-only implementation and passes with this fix.
- The patch applies without fuzz to the 7.2.5-4 sources for both kernel
  variants. Recipe checksums and checkpatch validation pass.

The original sign-off below is retained for provenance. It does not
indicate review or approval of these subsequent changes by the author.

Link: https://github.com/rs0x29a/Linux-on-HONOR-MagicBook-14-Pro-2026-AI_ZQC-P_M1010/commit/1f5be693c6dd9c0c1b8406fb85cbdbbe893b8b23

